  "_comment": [
    "Synthetic gen5 Black scenario (plan 2.7 for gen5; decision 6 says a recording needs Scott):",
    "a new game, the starter, a route change, one wild battle, the Cilan battle, a level up, a",
    "blackout and a reset. It is built to touch the hooks in gen5's mounted():",
    "  flags.new_game false -> true            new run (timer start, attempt++, set_options writes)",
    "  overworld.map_index change              map handling",
    "  battle.opponent.trainer set / unset     'IN - Cilan' / 'OUT - Cilan' markers (any transition)",
    "  meta.state 'From Battle' with a split trainer",
    "                                          Full/Deprecated/Simple split CSVs, prepare_for_splits",
    "  player.team.0.level change              level-up handling",
    "  battle.player.pkmn_ram.pokemon_0_ram.stats.hp -> 0 in Battle, then battle.other.battle",
    "  21828 -> -1893922566                    blackout (the Black/White pointer edge)",
    "  player.name 'SCOTT' -> '' with the timer running",
    "                                          reset (playerResets++, OBS 'RESET')",
    "The Striaton part starts at 62 s so the Cilan split lands after the timer's first minute",
    "(known-legacy-bugs.md #33 is gen4's, but gen5's timer text has the same shape). Referenced",
    "properties carry the glossary value the recorder would have written. Every path is checked",
    "against the mapper XML at build time. Values are plausible, not a real run: this fixture proves",
    "determinism and no-change-under-refactor, never correctness (see make-fixture.ts)."
